From 8d9a25d8fbf90c8dcc2eaa878db47badc2489ed8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Helmut Januschka <helmut@januschka.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:49:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] hires mic: gain the uplink and follow the recorder

The raw uplink decodes quiet enough to sound faint on a call, so each
frame now passes an envelope-tracked gain with a tanh limiter. Measured
on the same speech: RMS 116 before, 784 after.

The source is published for as long as the pods are connected, so an
app can select AirPodsHiRes before anything streams, and a one-second
poll arms the radio stream when a recorder appears and disarms it when
the last one leaves. Nothing is streamed while no app is listening.
An unknown capture query neither arms nor disarms, matching the rule
the A2DP path already follows.

Reader detection shares the existing capture query: its matcher is now
a parameter, since the hi-res source carries no address in its name.
